IMPORT `bmfire-exclusions`

-- How much is payable: the measure of each loss, then the conditions that reduce it, then
-- the deductible, then the caps. The provisions are spread over the Rules; each is here
-- under its own number:
--   preamble        the measure: value at the time of loss, amount of damage, or reinstatement
--   VII.3           reinstatement, and the cap on it
--   VIII.1(b)       the measure for electronic data processing media
--   III.2(b)        only the excess over a marine policy
--   VII.5           the average condition, item by item
--   VII.6           contribution with other insurance
--   proviso (i)-(ii) the caps, per item and for the claim
--   IV, and the closing paragraphs of E, F, G, H, I, J   the deductible
--
-- ORDER. Section IV fixes one step: the deductible comes "sau khi đã áp dụng tất cả các
-- điều kiện, điều khoản của hợp đồng này bao gồm cả điều kiện luật tỷ lệ" (after all the
-- conditions and terms, average included). The others are taken in the order a loss
-- adjuster would apply them: measure, marine excess, average, contribution, the per-item
-- cap; then the deductible; then the claim cap (fork F18).
--
-- This module computes the amount for losses it is handed. Which losses are covered is
-- decided in bmfire-claim.l4, which hands over only those.

§ `The amount payable`

§§ `VII.3 — reinstatement`

-- Bao Minh may repair or replace instead of paying, need not restore exactly, and in no
-- case pays for reinstatement more than the cost needed to restore the property to its
-- condition before the loss, or more than its sum insured.
